              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "White-haired and lightly haired individuals possible. with poorly pigmented skin.",
              "pdf_page": 466,
              "printed_page": 384,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Imiquimod 5% cream—induces local",
              "pdf_page": 466,
              "printed_page": 384,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "History of sunbathing. immune response; for individual lesions, esp.",
              "pdf_page": 466,
              "printed_page": 384,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Outdoor housing. actinic keratosis; apply q48h until resolution.",
              "pdf_page": 466,
              "printed_page": 384,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Regions with greater sun exposure, high",
              "pdf_page": 466,
              "printed_page": 384,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Cryosurgery—actinic keratosis, SCC. altitudes; usually occurs in summer, but also",
              "pdf_page": 466,
              "printed_page": 384,
              "column": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullet",
              "level": 0,
              "text": "Antibiotics—control secondary pyoderma in winter as result of reflection from snow. (see Pyoderma).",
              "pdf_page": 466,
              "printed_page": 384,
              "column": 2
            }
          ]
        }
