    "acknowledgment": "The author acknowledges dermis; coagulation necrosis. the prior contribution of Alexander H. Werner Resnick. TREATMENT •Sun avoidance—keep indoors during day; avoid reflected sunlight; apply waterproof (>30 SPF) sunscreen (without zinc oxide and PABA); sun-protective clothing. •Surgical excision of neoplastic lesions. MEDICATIONS DRUG(S) OF CHOICE •Cyclooxygenase-2 (COX2) inhibitors— overexpression by sun-damaged cells; inhibition of COX2 demonstrated improvement: firocoxib 5 mg/kg/day PO. •Glucocorticoids—reduced inflammation noted in acute cases; prednisolone 0.5–1 mg/FOLLOW-UP Clinical outcome and cyclo-oxygenase-2 expression in 5 dogs with solar dermatitis/actinic keratosis treated with firocoxib. Vet Dermatol 2013, 24(6):606–e147. protection. In: Kirk’s Current Veterinary Therapy XV. St. Louis, MO: Elsevier, 2014, pp. 480–482."
